            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito asked why the issue would be limited to a decision to plead guilty rather than a trial verdict."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2680d3fef795246349cdf4ba48574b87c70617184e33c0ef1dde61c780711ccd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2680d3fef795-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, justice Ginsburg questioned how the rule would cover the many possible consequences."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2680d3fef795246349cdf4ba48574b87c70617184e33c0ef1dde61c780711ccd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2680d3fef795-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 7,
              "start": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justice Scalia expressed concern about opening a \u201cPandora\u2019s box\u201d and whether the rule could be sensibly limited to deportation."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2680d3fef795246349cdf4ba48574b87c70617184e33c0ef1dde61c780711ccd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2680d3fef795-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy, justice Kennedy remarked that it seemed odd that the government would be at risk when counsel strays from professional responsibility."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2680d3fef795246349cdf4ba48574b87c70617184e33c0ef1dde61c780711ccd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2680d3fef795-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 36,
              "start": 36
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor asked how the defense\u2019s argument would be addressed if a trial could win the case."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2680d3fef795246349cdf4ba48574b87c70617184e33c0ef1dde61c780711ccd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2680d3fef795-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer asked whether counsel should inform a defendant about severe immigration consequences that could lead to death for the defendant and his family."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Long",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2680d3fef795246349cdf4ba48574b87c70617184e33c0ef1dde61c780711ccd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2680d3fef795-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Mr. Long argued that prevailing professional norms and ethical obligations in Kentucky do not address this type of situation."
      }
    ],
